Cornish (which died out in the 18th century but was revived in the 20th) ha=
s hardly a native speaker community. There are some isolated native speaker=
s who grew up with the language as their parents spoke it to them. But ther=
e are many revivalists who can speak and write the language, natively or no=
t.

